lium is a bacterial chromosome","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"7561bcf8-9460-5643-9e11-96265d6fd309","text":"They are pigments in chloroplasts","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"d1cc8946-fcfb-586a-ba2c-f97254276182","position":53,"prompt":"An organism is unicellular, has ribosomes and circular DNA but no membrane-bound nucleus. How should it be classified at the cell-type level?","explanation":"The absence of a membrane-bound nucleus with circular cellular DNA indicates a prokaryotic cell.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"hard","cognitive":"analysis","topic":"Classification and Diversity of Living Things","fingerprint":"dfe312761980f1748e5a1fbce706b2efbd82222b96a309ec6a7d8874753a8325","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"BIO 111 General Biology I module, Study Session 3","sourceKind":"supplied_bio111_material","reviewedFromLocalFile":true,"databaseCourseCode":"BIO 101","sourceCourseCode":"BIO 111"},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_bio101_from_bio111_300_v1","sourceReference":"BIO 111 General Biology I module, Study Session 3","technicalAccuracyReviewCompleted":true,"humanVerificationRequired":true},"options":[{"id":"cd5279e4-bbb6-5d89-9a04-d82cacc85c11","text":"Multicellular animal","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"67b7685f-8801-53eb-8208-b8e91764686e","text":"Fungal tissue","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"ee0af7d3-c890-568d-9258-40f81a2c3629","text":"Plant organ","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"669f68c3-7165-50f2-87af-19cc96fd985b","text":"Prokaryotic","isCorrect":true,"position":3}]},{"id":"1ea008c2-de46-5441-9108-d2f04ac4fa9b","position":54,"prompt":"An organism has chitinous walls, forms hyphae and absorbs digested nutrients. Which kingdom best fits?","explanation":"Chitin walls, hyphal growth and absorptive nutrition are diagnostic fungal characteristics.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"hard","cognitive":"analysis","topic":"Classification and Diversity of Living Things","fingerprint":"7d308247b09187cf6c96469b8992