ion commonly increase variation among offspring?","explanation":"Recombination, assortment and random gamete fusion reshuffle genetic information.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Sexual and Asexual Reproduction","fingerprint":"4a8ac8d9a1664e7cd1ce4e9ffe5264ca9b3976c47f9f5632c4c604a8bb4a9bc4","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"BIO 111 General Biology I module, Study Session 14","sourceKind":"supplied_bio111_material","reviewedFromLocalFile":true,"databaseCourseCode":"BIO 101","sourceCourseCode":"BIO 111"},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_bio101_from_bio111_300_v1","sourceReference":"BIO 111 General Biology I module, Study Session 14","technicalAccuracyReviewCompleted":true,"humanVerificationRequired":true},"options":[{"id":"ec34ceb5-1085-58b7-8950-a193fb1edc1f","text":"Meiosis and fertilization create new allele combinations","isCorrect":true,"position":0},{"id":"1c544ac6-1c66-5d1d-b534-62a281ac3c0c","text":"It copies one parental genome unchanged","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"8c827bd9-7204-5370-bd9e-e331b5620d32","text":"It prevents mutation","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"65acd289-b645-5463-9c35-abb101c1d462","text":"It removes independent assortment","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"40e35631-0d34-567a-a623-86fa94eb43e8","position":273,"prompt":"Why is parthenogenesis not the same as autogamy?","explanation":"The presence or absence of gamete fusion distinguishes the two processes.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"hard","cognitive":"analysis","topic":"Sexual and Asexual Reproduction","fingerprint":"b27d2299fc31f3b72a7afbe27fd32b6773cc684a0a7b132bc39495b1b668b5c8","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"BIO 111 General Biology I module, Study Session 14","sourceKind":"supplied_bio111_material","reviewedFromLocalFile":true,"databaseCourseCode":"BIO 101","sourceCourseCode":"BIO 111"},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_bio101_from_bio111_300_v1","sourceReference":"BIO 111 General Biology I module, S