","isCorrect":false,"position":2},{"id":"f71fdef7-6381-5591-8f7f-6aed56683af6","text":"A close, persistent association between different species","isCorrect":true,"position":3}]},{"id":"ca8f5373-3659-5b33-a6f4-e2c854d5efe9","position":290,"prompt":"Which prey feature can evolve under predation pressure?","explanation":"Predators select for traits that improve prey detection avoidance or defence.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Biological Interactions and Community Ecology","fingerprint":"95c52de078bce439caeb23226b6681d6c6d9260e69a34180a96e647cf27f36f1","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"BIO 111 General Biology I module, Study Session 15","sourceKind":"supplied_bio111_material","reviewedFromLocalFile":true,"databaseCourseCode":"BIO 101","sourceCourseCode":"BIO 111"},"generationMeta":{"import":"codex_bio101_from_bio111_300_v1","sourceReference":"BIO 111 General Biology I module, Study Session 15","technicalAccuracyReviewCompleted":true,"humanVerificationRequired":true},"options":[{"id":"82232486-61de-5d0e-b8e3-deadba0c251d","text":"Elimination of reproduction","isCorrect":false,"position":0},{"id":"ec61c0a3-6a78-5f9c-92aa-d3565aead0b1","text":"A bacterial nucleoid","isCorrect":false,"position":1},{"id":"69b242ff-3390-50ce-8d16-480c13389a2e","text":"Camouflage or warning coloration","isCorrect":true,"position":2},{"id":"95226c93-a067-50c9-86c2-483c3c2f65f1","text":"Loss of every sensory response","isCorrect":false,"position":3}]},{"id":"e3b781f1-4c6f-5de2-870e-789215d4a3f8","position":291,"prompt":"Nitrogen-fixing bacteria in legume root nodules illustrate which interaction?","explanation":"The plant receives usable nitrogen while bacteria receive resources and a protected habitat.","questionKind":"application","difficulty":"medium","cognitive":"application","topic":"Biological Interactions and Community Ecology","fingerprint":"3295416772cfda0b0cd024a777aec122442dde7cd5e03c40378e9f1916c00d9d","studyRef":{"sourceLabel":"BIO